  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "Given below are two statements:<br />Statement-I: An elevator can go up or down with uniform speed when its weight is balanced with the tension of its cable.<br />Statement-II: Force exerted by the floor of an elevator on the foot of a person standing on it is more than his/her weight when the elevator goes down with increasing speed.<br />In the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "SovI7",
      "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are false",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "kBpBq",
      "text": "Statement I is true but Statement II is false",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "tjI0o",
      "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are true",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "uF4zV",
      "text": "Statement I is false but Statement II is true",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/e6aca9ab-cab5-4483-8a22-08219f29eb74-9893421.PNG\" style=\"width: 65px; height: 150px;\" /></p><p>When elevator is moving with uniform speed <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></math>, as the net force along the vertical direction should be zero.</p><p>Therefore, Statement-I is true.</p><p>Now, when elevator is going down with increasing speed, its acceleration is downward.<br />Hence,&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Clearly, normal reaction is&nbsp;less than weight. So Statement-II is false.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
